1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Your API works. Anyone on earth can call it right now.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
Turn off plain HTTP. Not a redirect — off.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,800
Microsoft Entra ID validates the token. No token, no entry.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,600
A different question. Her token is valid; her rows are still only hers.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,400
Key Vault holds them. A managed identity fetches them. No password anywhere.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,200
Application Insights and Defender for Cloud. You see the attempt.

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,000
The call dies at step 2, and step 5 tells you it happened.

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,800
HTTPS first is not optional. Monitoring last is fine.
